    "created_at": "2022-03-15T07:19:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-15T07:19:56Z",
    "body": "I wasn't there when this was decided, but I think the intent is that the server can treat these status codes as \"trusted\" when the client is a browser. How useful this is in practice I'm not sure.\r\n\r\nIt would probably be good practice to use the private-use codes 4000 to 4015 as mirrors of the codes 1000 to 1015 for JavaScript client use.\r\n\r\n> 1003 would be useful at the very least for cases where the client can only accept binary frames or can only accept text frames.\r\n\r\nSpecifying the stream type in the constructor is something we might do for [WebSocketStream](https://github.com/ricea/websocketstream-explainer) in future.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
